<title>SINGAPORE: Eng Wah year net races 95 pct to S$1.3 mln.</title>
<headline>Eng Wah year net races 95 pct to S$1.3 mln.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-06-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year to March 31, 1997</p>
<p>		   (in millions of S$ unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net profit			     1.34  vs  0.69</p>
<p>    Dividend (cents)		     0.75  vs  0.50</p>
<p>    Group shr (cents)		    1.34  vs  0.69</p>
<p>    Turnover				15.15  vs 11.31</p>
<p>    Other income incl. interest	0.41  vs  0.55</p>
<p>    Depreciation (expense)	     1.47  vs  0.70</p>
<p>    Losses from associates	     0.06  vs  0.02</p>
<p>    Pre-tax profit			 2.36  vs  1.12</p>
<p>    Tax					0.90  vs  0.41</p>
<p>    Minorities		   (loss)  0.06  vs   nil</p>
<p>Dividend pay date: October 17, 1997</p>
<p>Last day books open: September 30, 1997</p>
<p>Note - Leisure group the Eng Wah Organisation said the opening of its redeveloped Jubilee Entertainment Complex had contributed substantially to the 95 percent rise in net earnings.</p>
<p>-- Singapore newsroom (65 8703199)</p>
</text>
